{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1248513-homebrewing-an-underworld","id":1248513,"title":"Homebrewing an Underworld","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-21T14:11:16-07:00","id":1248513,"title":"Homebrewing an Underworld","content":"Working off 3rd edition core and various snippets of conversation on the internet (I haven't read any previous books), I've had a vision forming in my head of what I'd like the Underworld to be, and I've written some of it out in the form of these notes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Underworld is a dreary place. It's shaped vaguely after Creation - mountains, seas, deserts, cities, etc. When something major feature of Creation changes, the Underworld 'grows' a facsimile. This is a slow process; a mimicry of a castle may take hundreds of years to grow.<br /> <br /> These things are usually not made of the same material as the things they are mimicking. A mimicry of a granite castle may be made of basalt or some unliving wood. A mimicry of a forest may be made of clay, and so on.<br /> <br /> Determined efforts by the inhabitants of the Underworld can easily keep these growths down.<br /> <br /> The Underworld is wetter than Creation, with the Underworld mimicries of prairies being more like bogs.<br /> <br /> There is nothing living, per se, in the Underworld - only the undead. But many animate things in the Underworld have never lived, and do not have equivalents in Creation.<br /> <br /> Most ghosts do not hold the intelligence and ability of the people they were, acting instead in their memories, behaving as they remember behaving, rarely if ever changing or learning anything new. But some ghosts hold on to more of what they were, and strive to learn and gain.<br /> The mechanism for this difference is not understood. Some believe it is a person's last moments that make the difference, or karma for how they lived, or some intrinsic part of who they are.<br /> <br /> The Underworld is largely ruled as small fiefdoms, each with their Lord in Death. Larger kingdoms consist of lesser lords with sworn fealty to greater ones.<br /> <br /> In the center of the Underworld is the Gate of Oblivion, on top of which is the festering remains of primordial beings, packed together as a region known as the Labyrinth. They scream and babble endlessly, driving those who near it insane. Still, whispers tell of unfathomable power and riches within it's depths, and foolhardy souls travel from all the Underworld to plumb it's depths. Very few return, and even fewer return intact.<br /> <br /> Recently, one particular soul returned with a great and terrible power. Using some Labyrinthine artifacts - of dead, primordial essence - he has fashioned an Exaltation. Even in it's deathly nature, however, it does not hold well to ghosts. So he traveled to Creation and found a living human on the edge of death, and offered it to him in return for his service.<br /> <br /> Truly a foolhardy soul, he shared this knowledge with other Deathlords. Many others have since journeyed into the Labyrinth to claim such power, and a few have returned. Some have been driven mad by the Labyrinth's whispers. Some of these mad spirits claim that an intelligence of the Labyrinth speaks to them, gives them power, and they use their newfound power in service of this intelligence, usually in pursuit of Oblivion. None are more feared and hated in the Underworld than these Oblivion Knights.<br /> <br /> Most Deathlords have enough on their hands managing their territory in the Underworld, but some - especially among those who have claimed power from the Labyrinth - now dream of conquest on Creation above.<br /> <br /> Manufacturing goods in the Underworld is a rare thing, as most material is weak, brittle, and nigh-impossible to work, but there are a few materials that are widely useful. Most of them are at least slightly magical.<br /> <br /> The most potent magical material is Blackblood, which flows in rivulets and collects in pools in the depths of the Underworld. There are widely-known techniques for forging this liquid into a metallic substance, usually for use in armor and weapons, and in some rich fiefdoms into coins.<br /> <br /> It is widely suspected that this substance originates from the Labyrinth - that it is the blood of those dead beings, hence the name.<br /> <br /> Successful mimicries of this material's properties have been made by smelting ghosts with stygian iron, creating a substance called Soulsteel, though this practice is generally frowned upon.<br /> <br /> The material Ghostsilk is used by Ghostsilk Spiders to catch and consume spirits, to sustain their animation. Food and hunger are not the same in the Underworld - not quite the same, but alike.<br /> <br /> Clever hunters and craftsmen gather and weave this material into clothing, baskets and such. Efforts to synthesize the material have had very limited success.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6893-drazhya","name":"Drazhya","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T12:43:17-07:00","id":1248998,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Looks like you have some good ideas, some not-so-good ideas, and you've fallen into a couple of traps that previous editions did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drazhya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1248513-homebrewing-an-underworld#post1248513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Underworld is a dreary place. It's shaped vaguely after Creation - mountains, seas, deserts, cities, etc. When something major feature of Creation changes, the Underworld 'grows' a facsimile. This is a slow process; a mimicry of a castle may take hundreds of years to grow.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should avoid &quot;dreary places&quot; as large as an entire dimension or no one will want to visit there. Just because the place isn't alive doesn't mean it can't be lively and interesting.<br /> <br /> Having the Underworld mirror Creation sounds good at first, but you will find that it will become a problem when you try to detail a kingdom of ghosts. You end up with souls from all different eras mashed into one region, making it difficult to describe a coherent culture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Underworld is wetter than Creation, with the Underworld mimicries of prairies being more like bogs. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> <br /> Why? This seems an odd detail.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the center of the Underworld is the Gate of Oblivion, on top of which is the festering remains of primordial beings, packed together as a region known as the Labyrinth. They scream and babble endlessly, driving those who near it insane. Still, whispers tell of unfathomable power and riches within it's depths, and foolhardy souls travel from all the Underworld to plumb it's depths. Very few return, and even fewer return intact. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You may have made your Labyrinth too dangerous. Players need to feel like the risk is worth the reward before they'll want to venture somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Recently, one particular soul returned with a great and terrible power. Using some Labyrinthine artifacts - of dead, primordial essence - he has fashioned an Exaltation. Even in it's deathly nature, however, it does not hold well to ghosts. So he traveled to Creation and found a living human on the edge of death, and offered it to him in return for his service. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> <br /> Getting rid of the mirror nature of the Solar and Abyssal Exaltations strips them of a lot of the automatic flavoring they currently possess. If you do that, you are going to have to build a lot of interest in them by other means. Do you have any plans for how to fill that gap?<br /> <br /> </span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Truly a foolhardy soul, he shared this knowledge with other Deathlords. Many others have since journeyed into the Labyrinth to claim such power, and a few have returned. Some have been driven mad by the Labyrinth's whispers. Some of these mad spirits claim that an intelligence of the Labyrinth speaks to them, gives them power, and they use their newfound power in service of this intelligence, usually in pursuit of Oblivion. None are more feared and hated in the Underworld than these Oblivion Knights. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You are laying the ground work for the same problem that plagued Abyssals in 2nd Edition. If the Deathlords and Abyssals are working to destroy Creation in a coherent fashion, then you end up with Deathlords that must be destroyed and Abyssals who are either evil nihilists or <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0044.html\" target=\"_blank\">Drizzt-style</a> &quot;struggling to redeem themselves&quot; anti-heroes. Those are nice to play once or twice, but it gets old eventually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Manufacturing goods in the Underworld is a rare thing, as most material is weak, brittle, and nigh-impossible to work, but there are a few materials that are widely useful. Most of them are at least slightly magical. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><br /> <br /> This is going to hurt you in the long run. The Underworld matters only when it has an impact on Creation. If the only things you can really get out of the Underworld is soulsteel and the biggest interactions it has with Creation are Deathlords and Abyssals trying to conquer or subvert kingdoms, then your players won't venture into the Underworld in any other capacity than as a big dungeon, there to kill the boss and loot the corpses for treasure.<br /> <br /> Economic ties are one of the primary ways to connect Creation and the Underworld in a peaceful manner.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The most potent magical material is Blackblood, which flows in rivulets and collects in pools in the depths of the Underworld. There are widely-known techniques for forging this liquid into a metallic substance, usually for use in armor and weapons, and in some rich fiefdoms into coins.<br /> ...<br /> Successful mimicries of this material's properties have been made by smelting ghosts with stygian iron, creating a substance called Soulsteel, though this practice is generally frowned upon. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This sounds like an attempt to make &quot;no tortured souls&quot; soulsteel. That steals thunder from soutsteel and has less narrative weight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is widely suspected that this substance originates from the Labyrinth - that it is the blood of those dead beings, hence the name. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nice idea, but probably best to apply this thought to the ore that is one of the primary ingredients in soulsteel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The material Ghostsilk is used by Ghostsilk Spiders to catch and consume spirits, to sustain their animation. Food and hunger are not the same in the Underworld - not quite the same, but alike. </div> </div> </div>I'd like to hear more about these spiders. What do they look like in your mind? My mind conjures images of something unlike a natural spider and more like a marionette, with a dozen wooden legs pulled by silk strings and no discernible head.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T12:45:26-07:00","id":1248999,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Double post. Forum decided to be flaky for me.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5